# Testing Rules

Test business behavior, not only implementation details.

Unit tests should cover:

- Business rules
- State transitions
- Permission decisions
- Calculations

Integration tests should cover:

- Database behavior
- Transactions
- Tenant isolation
- API contracts

E2E tests should cover representative user workflows.

Every security-sensitive feature must include negative tests.

Minimum tenant test pattern:

Tenant A user
→ cannot access Tenant B resource

A feature is not done when CRUD works. It is done when validation, authorization, tenant isolation, UX states, business rules, and relevant tests work.
